      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the volumes of the two cubes and then find the ratio of these volumes.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches\nThe volume \\( V \\) of a cube is given by the formula:\n\\[\nV = s^3\n\\]\nwhere \\( s \\) is the length of an edge of the cube.\n\nFor the first cube with an edge length of 6 inches:\n\\[\ns = 6 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\\[\nV_1 = 6^3 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot\nFirst, we need to convert the edge length from feet to inches because the volume is given in cubic inches. There are 12 inches in a foot.\n\n\\[\ns = 1 \\text{ foot} = 12 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate the volume:\n\\[\nV_2 = 12^3 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the ratio of the volumes\nThe ratio \\( R \\) of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube is:\n\\[\nR = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Simplify the ratio\nTo simplify \\(\\frac{216}{1728}\\), we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. The GCD of 216 and 1728 is 216.\n\nDivide both the numerator and the denominator by 216:\n\\[\n\\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\n\\]",
